{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794560100211,"sessionID":"ses_e2be2a3a9ffeGLGI0J0gF3MK6h","part":{"partID":"prt_1d41e03d8001rTbk3UaHvEsyWx","sessionID":"ses_e2be2a3a9ffeGLGI0J0gF3MK6h","messageID":"msg_1d41de784001IqzBvJblRP6mwP","type":"tool","id":"call_716fcb6028bf40ca9833d14f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs","limit":60},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, lines 1-60\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Shipped Instruction Check Engine\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // A repository that took the shipped instruction template can be in any of seven\n8: // states, and nothing in it says which one. Its shipped sections may be current, one\n9: // release behind, or edited in place; its own content may sit in the marked block or be\n10: // scattered between shipped sections; it may have no root document at all. Without that\n11: // answer there is nothing to plan a rewrite from, and no way to tell a safe replacement\n12: // from one that would drop a line somebody wrote. So this engine reports, per row and\n13: // without writing a byte, what the repository holds against the manifest.\n14: //\n15: // Three of the twelve rows are answers this engine must not invent. The delivery budget\n16: // and its anchors belong to the rule-copy canary, the Cursor pointer block belongs to\n17: // the gate 1 sync, and the router belongs to the repo-rules checker. Each already has\n18: // tests and an owner, so each is run as a child process and its own lines are carried\n19: // into the report; re-deriving any of them here would be a second opinion that drifts\n20: // from the first. The rest are pure classifiers over one read of the target tree.\n21: //\n22: // The run is read-only by construction: the only paths it opens for reading are under\n23: // the target root plus the manifest, and the three child tools it runs are read-only\n24: // modes. A repository that cannot be classified at all (no manifest, no target\n25: // directory, an unreadable root document) is a failed precondition and exits 2, because\n26: // an empty report would read like a clean one.\n27: //\n28: // Usage: agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--manifest <path>] [--source] [--json]\n29: //   --root <dir>      classify this repository instead of the one this script ships in\n30: //   --manifest <path> read this manifest instead of the shipped one\n31: //   --source          run the template-purity row even outside the source repository\n32: //   --json            print one JSON object instead of the text report\n33: // Exit codes: 0 nothing to report, 1 at least one finding or an unproven row,\n34: //             2 a precondition failed\n35: \n36: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: // 1. IMPORTS\n38: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n39: \n40: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n41: const fs = require('node:fs');\n42: const path = require('node:path');\n43: \n44: const {\n45:   classifyBody,\n46:   deliveryAnchorEnd,\n47:   matchSections,\n48:   segment,\n49: } = require('./lib/agents-md-sections.cjs');\n50: const { sourceStatus } = require('./agents-md-manifest.cjs');\n51: \n52: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n53: // 2. CONSTANTS\n54: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n55: \n56: const TAG = '[agents-md-check]';\n57: const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '../../../..');\n58: const MANIFEST_PATH = path.resolve(__dirname, '../assets/agents-md-manifest.json');\n59: const GENERATOR = path.resolve(__dirname, 'agents-md-manifest.cjs');\n60: // The router checker ships beside the skill that authors rules, and the manifest links\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, lines 1-60\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Shipped Instruction Check Engine\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // A repository that took the shipped instruction template can be in any of seven\n8: // states, and nothing in it says which one. Its shipped sections may be current, one\n9: // release behind, or edited in place; its own content may sit in the marked block or be\n10: // scattered between shipped sections; it may have no root document at all. Without that\n11: // answer there is nothing to plan a rewrite from, and no way to tell a safe replacement\n12: // from one that would drop a line somebody wrote. So this engine reports, per row and\n13: // without writing a byte, what the repository holds against the manifest.\n14: //\n15: // Three of the twelve rows are answers this engine must not invent. The delivery budget\n16: // and its anchors belong to the rule-copy canary, the Cursor pointer block belongs to\n17: // the gate 1 sync, and the router belongs to the repo-rules checker. Each already has\n18: // tests and an owner, so each is run as a child process and its own lines are carried\n19: // into the report; re-deriving any of them here would be a second opinion that drifts\n20: // from the first. The rest are pure classifiers over one read of the target tree.\n21: //\n22: // The run is read-only by construction: the only paths it opens for reading are under\n23: // the target root plus the manifest, and the three child tools it runs are read-only\n24: // modes. A repository that cannot be classified at all (no manifest, no target\n25: // directory, an unreadable root document) is a failed precondition and exits 2, because\n26: // an empty report would read like a clean one.\n27: //\n28: // Usage: agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--manifest <path>] [--source] [--json]\n29: //   --root <dir>      classify this repository instead of the one this script ships in\n30: //   --manifest <path> read this manifest instead of the shipped one\n31: //   --source          run the template-purity row even outside the source repository\n32: //   --json            print one JSON object instead of the text report\n33: // Exit codes: 0 nothing to report, 1 at least one finding or an unproven row,\n34: //             2 a precondition failed\n35: \n36: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: // 1. IMPORTS\n38: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n39: \n40: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n41: const fs = require('node:fs');\n42: const path = require('node:path');\n43: \n44: const {\n45:   classifyBody,\n46:   deliveryAnchorEnd,\n47:   matchSections,\n48:   segment,\n49: } = require('./lib/agents-md-sections.cjs');\n50: const { sourceStatus } = require('./agents-md-manifest.cjs');\n51: \n52: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n53: // 2. CONSTANTS\n54: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n55: \n56: const TAG = '[agents-md-check]';\n57: const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '../../../..');\n58: const MANIFEST_PATH = path.resolve(__dirname, '../assets/agents-md-manifest.json');\n59: const GENERATOR = path.resolve(__dirname, 'agents-md-manifest.cjs');\n60: // The router checker ships beside the skill that authors rules, and the manifest links\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs\",\"limit\":60}"},"time":{"start":1794560099288,"end":1794560100211}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794560100215,"sessionID":"ses_e2be2a3a9ffeGLGI0J0gF3MK6h","part":{"partID":"prt_1d41e0589001GQHVcH25wuZCqk","sessionID":"ses_e2be2a3a9ffeGLGI0J0gF3MK6h","messageID":"msg_1d41de784001IqzBvJblRP6mwP","type":"tool","id":"call_4e6404d615f6494c9dbe924c","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown","pattern":"agents-md-(check|embed)"},"output":"Found 12 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:\n  Line 33: +-- agents-md-check.cjs\n\n  Line 34: +-- agents-md-embed.cjs\n\n  Line 102: | `agents-md-check.cjs` | The read-only AGENTS.md check: twelve rows reporting the install state, the sections lost or reordered, the currency of each body, every pin, the delivery budget, the shape of the repository block, the repository's own content and its local edits, each runtime copy, the `REPO RULES.md` router and the source template's purity. Three of them run their owner as a child instead of re-deriving it, carrying the rule-copy canary's budget lines, the gate 1 pointer sync's Cursor block and the repo-rules checker's summary. `--root <dir>` classifies another repository and `--json` prints the same report for a machine. A row it cannot prove reads `UNKNOWN` rather than `PASS`, so it exits 0 on no finding, 1 on a finding or an unproven row and 2 on a failed precondition. |\n\n  Line 103: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | The writing half of `/doctor:agents-md`, in three subcommands. `plan` composes every target in memory and prints the targets, the diffs, the new block, the byte budget, the preservation ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest, and writes nothing. `apply --plan-digest <digest>` recomposes, refuses a digest the tree no longer produces, backs up every path it will touch, writes only inside the allowlist it checks in code and then proves the composition against the bytes on disk, restoring from the backup and ending `STATUS=FAIL` when one line went missing. `restore --run=<dir>` puts back exactly the paths that run's `manifest.json` records, removes the files, and the empty folders, that run created, and keeps the backup. It exits 0 when there was nothing to do or the work finished, 1 on a failed proof or a declined run and 2 on a failed precondition or a path outside the allowlist. |\n\n  Line 104: | `agents-md-manifest.cjs` | Generates and gates the shipped manifest's `derived` key: a copy of every shipped body, its hash and the router rows, taken from the root documents. `--write` refreshes it and `--check` is the freshness gate, so a body that drifted from the template fails here instead of surfacing as a check finding. It refuses a heading no authored entry matches, an authored entry that matches nothing, and text above the first heading, and `--write` runs only in the repository that ships the template. Each of the three engines has its own suite: `agents-md-check.test.cjs`, `agents-md-embed.test.cjs` and `agents-md-manifest.test.cjs`, driven from the recipe folders under `tests/fixtures/agents-md/`. |\n\n  Line 171: | `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--json]` | Report the twelve AGENTS.md rows for this repository or another one, and write nothing. |\n\n  Line 172: | `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan [--root <dir>] [--keep-claude-md] [--create-router]` | Print every target with its diff, the new block, the budget, the preservation ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest. Writes nothing, and prints `NOTHING TO DO` when the repository is already in its target state. |\n\n  Line 173: | `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest <digest> [--root <dir>]` | Back up, write inside the allowlist and prove the composition, only with the digest the plan printed. |\n\n  Line 174: | `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs restore --run=<dir> --yes` | Put back exactly the paths one run recorded, and remove the files, and the empty folders, that run created. |\n\n  Line 231: | `agents-md-check.cjs` | Read-only over any root: it reads the instruction file, its runtime copies and `REPO RULES.md`, runs three owner tools as children in their check-only forms and writes nothing. |\n\n  Line 232: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | `plan` is read-only. `apply` writes only the paths in its own allowlist, all of them under the target root, after backing each one up under `.skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<digest>/` (or the OS temp folder when that path is not ignored), and restores from that backup itself when its post-write proof fails. `restore` writes only the paths the run's `manifest.json` records and keeps the backup folder. It never runs `git add`, `git commit` or `git stash`. |\n\n  Line 257: | `agents-md-check.cjs` | `--root <dir>`. It also takes `--manifest <path>` and `--source` |\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":12,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 12 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:\n  Line 33: +-- agents-md-check.cjs\n\n  Line 34: +-- agents-md-embed.cjs\n\n  Line 102: | `agents-md-check.cjs` | The read-only AGENTS.md check: twelve rows reporting the install state, the sections lost or reordered, the currency of each body, every pin, the delivery budget, the shape of the repository block, the repository's own content and its local edits, each runtime copy, the `REPO RULES.md` router and the source template's purity. Three of them run their owner as a child instead of re-deriving it, carrying the rule-copy canary's budget lines, the gate 1 pointer sync's Cursor block and the repo-rules checker's summary. `--root <dir>` classifies another repository and `--json` prints the same rep